From: Inga Pilchin <inga.pilchin@realsenseai.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] realsense: media-bus code for H.264 over the 8-bit carrier

H.264 rides the same opaque 8-bit CSI carrier as the variable-length row
added by the previous patch, but keeps a code of its own so the capture
node offers H.264 and JPEG as distinct, selectable formats. JPEG reuses
MEDIA_BUS_FMT_JPEG_1X8, and both use standard pixel formats.

Signed-off-by: Inga Pilchin <inga.pilchin@realsenseai.com>
---
diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h b/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h
index 90d71ce..d733896 100644
--- a/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/media-bus-format.h
@@ -170,6 +170,10 @@
  * up to the declared height, over an opaque 8-bit CSI carrier */
 #define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RS_VARLEN_1X8		0x500a
 
+/* RealSense H.264 over the opaque 8-bit carrier: own code so H.264 and JPEG
+ * stay separately selectable at the capture node. */
+#define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RS_H264_1X8		0x500b
+
 /* HSV - next is	0x6002 */
 #define MEDIA_BUS_FMT_AHSV8888_1X32		0x6001
 
